    "question": "What is tax-loss harvesting, and is it actually worth doing for an average investor?",
    "summary": "Tax-loss harvesting is the practice of selling investments at a loss to offset capital gains (and, within limits, ordinary income), thereby reducing current-year taxes while staying invested through a comparable replacement security. It can add meaningful after-tax value for higher-income investors…",
